{"case_id":"C097","maintenance_needed":false,"confidence":99,"change_types":["internal_refactor","constant_deduplication","formatting_cleanup"],"affected_functions":["do_dump","json_object_deep_copy","json_array_deep_copy"],"reason":"The commit only replaces three equivalent stack-buffer length expressions with the shared internal macro LOOP_KEY_LEN and fixes indentation. It does not introduce functionality, alter an entry point or public API, change initialization or configuration, or impose new input constraints. The existing harness continues to exercise do_dump through json_dumps and json_dump_callback with fuzz-controlled dump flags; no harness adaptation is required for this internal refactor.","evidence":["jansson_private.h defines LOOP_KEY_LEN as 2 + (sizeof(json_t *) * 2) + 1, preserving the stated space for \"0x\", a pointer rendered in hexadecimal, and a terminator.","dump.c changes only char loop_key[2 + (sizeof(json) * 2) + 1] to char loop_key[LOOP_KEY_LEN] inside do_dump.","value.c makes the corresponding buffer-expression replacement in json_object_deep_copy and json_array_deep_copy; their calls to jsonp_loop_check and surrounding behavior remain unchanged.","The harness already invokes both json_dumps and json_dump_callback after json_loadb, so the changed object-dumping path remains reachable with fuzz-controlled JSON input and flags."],"recommended_action":"Keep the existing fuzz harness unchanged; no new entry point, protocol, setup, configuration, or input generation is needed for this commit."}
